Drop the shell indirection from the exported variables

The driver's top-level Makefile turns on export-all (a bare `export`, line 66)
and then defines twelve variables as `?= $(shell echo $(SOMETHING))`. Under
kbuild that combination is quadratic: make rebuilds the exported environment
before every $(shell ...) call, and each rebuild walks the whole variable set
looking for recursive values it must not expand. The kernel build issues
thousands of $(shell ...) calls -- cc-option alone accounts for dozens -- so a
`make M=<dir> modules` burns CPU indefinitely without emitting a single
`CC [M]` line. With `make -d` it is unmistakable: 388k lines in thirty seconds,
almost all of them

  Makefile:67: not recursively expanding SDIO_HOST to export to shell function

`$(shell echo $(X))` is `$(X)` with the whitespace squeezed, and none of these
values contain anything a shell would transform, so expanding them directly is
equivalent and leaves nothing recursive in the exported set. The module then
builds in about two minutes.

Fixing the variables rather than removing the `export` keeps the change to the
smallest thing that is actually wrong: Makefile.build.kernel reads several of
these from the environment, and this tree passes the CONFIG_ATBM_* values on
the command line, where make exports them regardless.

Signed-off-by: John Chia <john@johnchia.com>

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -64,18 +64,18 @@
 endif
 
 export
-SDIO_HOST      ?= $(shell echo $(CONFIG_ATBM_SDIO_MMCx))
-IF1NAME        ?= $(shell echo $(CONFIG_ATBM_WIFIIF1_NAME))
-IF2NAME        ?= $(shell echo $(CONFIG_ATBM_WIFIIF2_NAME))
-FW             ?= $(shell echo $(CONFIG_ATBM_FW_NAME))
-MODULES_NAME   ?= $(shell echo $(CONFIG_ATBM_MODULE_NAME))
-USBVID		   ?= $(shell echo $(CONFIG_ATBM_USB_VID))
-USBPID		   ?= $(shell echo $(CONFIG_ATBM_USB_PID))
-SDIOVID			?=$(shell echo $(CONFIG_ATBM_SDIO_VID))
-SDIOPID			?=$(shell echo $(CONFIG_ATBM_SDIO_PID))
-MODDRVNAME	   ?= $(shell echo $(CONFIG_ATBM_MODULE_DRIVER_NAME))
-PLFDEVNAME	   ?= $(shell echo $(CONFIG_ATBM_PLATFORM_DEVICE_NAME))
-MODPMSTAYAWK   ?= $(shell echo $(CONFIG_ATBM_MODULE_PM_STAYAWK))
+SDIO_HOST      ?= $(CONFIG_ATBM_SDIO_MMCx)
+IF1NAME        ?= $(CONFIG_ATBM_WIFIIF1_NAME)
+IF2NAME        ?= $(CONFIG_ATBM_WIFIIF2_NAME)
+FW             ?= $(CONFIG_ATBM_FW_NAME)
